    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d205">

                <pb facs="0203" n="193" xml:id="pg193"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01/11–1549: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Second Secretary of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bacon</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-11-15T09:00:00+08:00">November 15,
                            1949—9 a. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 14—11:03 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2427. ReDepintel November 10.<anchor n="23" xml:id="d205-f1"/> Our impression is
                    that Titoism arose in Yugoslavia not because of any action or failure to act on
                    part of Western Powers, but as direct results of action injurious to Yugoslav
                    political independence and economic reconstruction. We consider estrangement
                    between China and USSR will probably arise in same way and our recognition at
                    this time could contribute little or nothing to this development.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bacon</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
